---
// Landing page. Design brief and research: docs/site.md. Every claim here must be
// something the app does today (docs/tracker.md), and the payment in "What the chain
// sees" is the real testnet payment from the 2026-09-30 dry run.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { downloadUrl, sourceUrl } from '../config';

const specUrl = `${sourceUrl}/blob/main/spec.md`;

const txid = 'e6ccd6b707e8ee7ed8b261855272dba317495afa6659e393d3f1691e9eef0237';

const path = [
  {
    icon: 'edit',
    title: 'A member proposes',
    text: "Recipient, amount and memo go into the vault's shared log, encrypted so only members can read it.",
  },
  {
    icon: 'endpoint',
    title: 'The relay passes it on',
    text: "A postbox for sealed envelopes. It can delay mail, but it can't open it, forge it or sign anything.",
  },
  {
    icon: 'check_circle',
    title: 'Each phone checks it',
    text: 'Your phone checks the transaction against the vault’s own keys, then asks you.',
    needsYou: true,
  },
  {
    icon: 'users',
    title: 'Enough members approve',
    text: 'Approving signs on the spot. By default, the approval that completes the threshold also sends the payment.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'globe',
    title: 'One ordinary signature',
    text: 'The shares combine into a single spend authorization. The network sees a normal shielded payment.',
  },
];

const extras = [
  { icon: 'plus', title: 'Batch payments', text: 'Up to 50 recipients in one proposal, typed or imported from a CSV, each with its own memo.' },
  { icon: 'time', title: 'An approval window', text: 'Proposals expire after 1, 3, 7 or 14 days, chosen when the vault is created.' },
  { icon: 'tor', title: 'Tor, fail-closed', text: 'Turn it on and every connection to the relay and the Zcash server goes through Tor, or doesn’t happen.' },
  { icon: 'eye', title: 'A viewing key for auditors', text: 'Hand an auditor the vault’s full history without the power to spend.' },
  { icon: 'history', title: 'History as CSV', text: 'Exported on your phone, with who proposed and who approved each payment.' },
  { icon: 'lock', title: 'Encrypted backups', text: 'A passphrase-protected file with your share of the vault. Restore it on a new phone.' },
  { icon: 'unlock', title: 'Unlock to sign', text: 'Biometrics or the screen lock before you propose, approve or send.' },
  { icon: 'wallet', title: 'Several vaults', text: 'Each with a fresh member identity, so the relay can’t link them to one person.' },
];

const limits = [
  ['Testnet only.', 'Zafe hasn’t had an external security audit. Mainnet waits for one.'],
  ['Android only, for now.', 'No iPhone app yet, and no hardware-wallet signers.'],
  ['Members see everything.', 'Every member can see the vault’s whole history, including after they leave. Removing someone completely means moving the funds to a new vault.'],
  ['Lost shares stay lost.', 'If more members lose their phones and backups than the vault can spare, the funds can’t be spent again. Nobody can recover them, Zafe included.'],
  ['The relay sees metadata.', 'Which mailboxes get messages, when, how large, and from which IP address. Tor hides the address.'],
];
---

<Base
  title="Zafe: a shielded multisig for Zcash"
  description="A shared Zcash wallet for grant committees, DAOs and small teams. A payment leaves only when enough members approve it on their own phones, and the chain sees an ordinary shielded transaction."
  bodyClass="home"
>
  <header class="bar">
    <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Zafe home">
      <img src="/assets/zafe.svg" alt="" width="28" height="28" />
      <span>zafe</span>
    </a>
    <nav aria-label="Page">
      <a href="#chain">What the chain sees</a>
      <a href="#path">How a payment moves</a>
      <a href="#limits">Limits</a>
      <a href={sourceUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Source</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>Nothing leaves the vault until enough of you approve&nbsp;it.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Zafe is a shared Zcash wallet for grant committees, DAOs and small teams. The
          members&rsquo; phones hold the vault together, and each one checks a payment
          before it signs. The chain sees an ordinary shielded payment.
        </p>
        <p class="cta">
          <a class="button" href={downloadUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Download for Android</a>
          <a class="link" href={specUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the spec</a>
        </p>
        <p class="status">Testnet only. Not yet externally audited. Open source, MIT or Apache-2.0.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-shot">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/assets/screens/approval_dark.webp" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
          <img
            src="/assets/screens/approval_light.webp"
            width="780"
            height="1136"
            alt="A 12.50 TAZ payment waiting for approvals: one of the two needed so far. You: waiting. One member approved, one waiting."
          />
        </picture>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="chain" class="block">
      <div class="grid head">
        <h2>A multisig the chain can&rsquo;t see</h2>
        <p>
          Zcash&rsquo;s shielded pool has no smart contracts to hold a rule like &ldquo;two of
          three must sign&rdquo;. Zafe uses FROST threshold signatures instead: each phone holds
          a share of the spending key, and enough shares make one ordinary signature. This
          is a real payment from our testnet trial, as the members saw it and as the chain
          recorded it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid views">
        <figure class="view members">
          <figcaption>What the members saw</figcaption>
          <p class="amount">0.01 <span>TAZ</span></p>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Proposed by</dt><dd>Member B, from the command-line client</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Approved by</dt><dd>Member C, then the phone</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Sent by</dt><dd>The phone, when its approval completed 2 of 3</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Fee</dt><dd>0.0001 TAZ</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Vault after</dt><dd>0.1149 TAZ</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </figure>

        <figure class="view chain">
          <figcaption>What Zcash testnet recorded</figcaption>
          <dl class="mono">
            <div><dt>Transaction</dt><dd class="hash">{txid}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Block</dt><dd>4,422,289</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Format</dt><dd>v6, Ironwood pool</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Size</dt><dd>9,166 bytes</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Fee</dt><dd>0.0001 TAZ</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Expires at</dt><dd>block 4,430,448</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="absent">
            Not on the chain: the amount, the recipient, the memo, the vault&rsquo;s balance,
            how many members it has, or that it&rsquo;s a multisig at all.
          </p>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <table class="compare">
        <caption>Compared with a multisig on Ethereum</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Safe on Ethereum</th><th scope="col">Zafe on Zcash</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">The rule lives in</th><td>A contract on-chain</td><td>The members&rsquo; key shares</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Public on-chain</th><td>Owners, threshold, every payment</td><td>An ordinary shielded transaction</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Who sees the balance</th><td>Anyone</td><td>Members, and anyone they give a viewing key</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Lost keys below the threshold</th><td>Funds stuck</td><td>Funds lost for good</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="path" class="block tall">
      <div class="grid head">
        <h2>How a payment moves</h2>
        <p>
          Members don&rsquo;t need to be online at the same time. Proposals, approvals and
          signature shares travel through a relay as sealed envelopes, and each phone does
          its part when it&rsquo;s opened or woken by a notification.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="path">
        {path.map((step) => (
          <li class:list={[{ 'needs-you': step.needsYou }]}>
            <span class="node"><Icon name={step.icon} /></span>
            <h3>{step.title}</h3>
            <p>{step.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <div class="grid relay">
        <p class="relay-label">The relay, exactly</p>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Can see</dt><dd>Mailbox ids, members&rsquo; public keys, IP addresses, when messages are sent and how large they are.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Can&rsquo;t see</dt><dd>Balances, addresses, amounts, recipients, memos, proposals, viewing keys or key shares.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Can&rsquo;t do</dt><dd>Spend, read content, or forge a member&rsquo;s message or vote. Gaps and reordering in the vault&rsquo;s log are detected.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block grid check">
      <figure class="check-shot">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/assets/screens/check_dark.webp" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
          <img
            src="/assets/screens/check_light.webp"
            width="780"
            height="840"
            loading="lazy"
            alt="Checked on this device: Matches. Below it, the Approve and sign button: approving signs the payment on this device."
          />
        </picture>
      </figure>
      <div class="check-copy">
        <h2>Your phone checks before it signs</h2>
        <p>
          In February 2025, signers of a large Ethereum multisig approved what their
          wallet&rsquo;s web page showed as a routine transfer. The page had been tampered with,
          and the funds went elsewhere.
          <a href="https://www.certora.com/blog/bybit-hack-multisig-wallet-security" rel="noopener noreferrer">How the Bybit theft worked</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          There&rsquo;s no web page in Zafe&rsquo;s signing path. Your phone takes the proposed
          transaction apart and checks it against the vault&rsquo;s own keys: every output is
          either exactly a payment in the proposal (recipient, amount and memo) or change
          back to the vault, every input is the vault&rsquo;s own money, and the fee is the
          standard fee. It works out what to sign by itself. If anything differs, it
          won&rsquo;t sign.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block grid setup">
      <div class="setup-copy">
        <h2>Every phone holds a share. None holds the key.</h2>
        <p>
          Pick the rule when you create a vault: any threshold from 2 of 2 up to 15
          members. Invite people with a link or a QR code. Their phones run a key ceremony
          together through the relay, and members compare a safety number so nobody can
          sit in the middle. Then each person saves an encrypted backup of their share.
        </p>
        <table class="holds">
          <caption>What each phone holds</caption>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">A key share</th><td>Unique to that phone. It can&rsquo;t spend on its own.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">The vault&rsquo;s viewing secret</th><td>The same on every phone. It sees all activity and can&rsquo;t spend.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">An identity key</th><td>Signs and seals this member&rsquo;s messages to the others.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <figure class="setup-art">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/assets/screens/key_shards_dark.webp" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
          <img src="/assets/screens/key_shards_light.webp" width="1080" height="740" loading="lazy" alt="" />
        </picture>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <div class="grid head">
        <h2>Also in the app</h2>
        <p>Everything here works on testnet today.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="extras">
        {extras.map((item) => (
          <li>
            <Icon name={item.icon} />
            <p><b>{item.title}.</b> {item.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="limits" class="block">
      <div class="grid head">
        <h2>Limits, before you trust it with anything</h2>
        <p>Read these before you put money in a vault. Some will change; the last three come with the design.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="limits">
        {limits.map(([title, text]) => (
          <li><b>{title}</b> {text}</li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="block grid open">
      <h2>Built in the open</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          The app, the relay and the protocol spec are on GitHub under MIT or Apache-2.0.
          Zafe builds on upstream libraries: <code>zcash_client_backend</code> and
          <code>orchard</code> for the wallet and Ironwood, <code>frost-core</code> with the
          RedPallas ciphersuite for threshold signatures, and <code>arti</code> for Tor. It adds
          no new cryptographic primitives.
        </p>
        <p>
          Made by <a href="https://github.com/AnmolBansalDEV" rel="noopener noreferrer">Anmol Bansal</a>.
          Questions and bug reports go to <a href={`${sourceUrl}/issues`} rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub issues</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block grid try">
      <h2>Try it on testnet</h2>
      <div>
        <p>You need two or three Android phones and a little testnet ZEC (TAZ) from a faucet.</p>
        <ol class="steps-plain">
          <li>Install Zafe on each phone.</li>
          <li>One person creates a vault and shares the invite. The others join from it.</li>
          <li>Send TAZ to the vault&rsquo;s address, propose a payment, and approve it from two phones.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="cta">
          <a class="button" href={downloadUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Download for Android</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="foot">
    <p>This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics and loads nothing from other servers.</p>
    <p>
      <a href={sourceUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Source</a>
      <a href={specUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Spec</a>
      <span>MIT or Apache-2.0</span>
    </p>
  </footer>
</Base>
